Pike 9.1: Changes since Pike 9.0
----------------------------------------------------------------------

New language features
---------------------

o Syntax for default values in multi-assignment.

  It is now possible to specify default values in multi-
  assignment.

    [int a, int b = a + 4] = ({ 1 });

  or

    [int a, int b = a + 4] = ({ 1, UNDEFINED });

  Both of the above statements will assign the value 1 to
  the variable a, and the value 5 to the variable b.

o Syntax for using multi-assign in function calls.

  *CAVEAT* Broken in combination with default values (Issue #10169).


Bug fixes
---------

o Concurrent.Future

  delay() now preserves an explicitly assigned backend throughout its
  internal callback chain, avoiding a dependency on the default backend.

o predef::backtrace()

  Improved handling of frames whose arguments are not fully initialized.

o predef::{en,de}code_value()

  Several fixes related to encoding and decoding of programs.

o Cpp

  - Fixed line numbering issue when handling multi-line comments
    in arguments to macros.

  - Improved cleanup when preprocessor callbacks throw errors.

o Compiler

  - Keep mutable container construction visible to the normal optimizer.
    This restores array append optimizations and avoids replacing simple
    array allocation with expensive recursive copies of constants.

o Runtime

o Operator functions


Incompatible changes
--------------------


New modules and functions
-------------------------



New features
------------

o Compiler

  SSA-enabled builds now enable integer-region optimizations by default
  on AMD64 and SPARC64 with 64-bit Pike integers. Set the environment
  variable PIKE_SSA_NO_INTEGER_REGIONS=1 to disable them.

  SPARC32 now also supports integer regions with 32-bit Pike integers.


